.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt RMXOS-INSTALL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rmxos-install
.Nd write a whole fresh rmxOS disk from a full stream
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -disk Ar disk
.Fl -catalog Ar DIR | URL
.Fl -hostname Ar name
.Fl -user Ar name
.Fl -key Ar file
.Fl -console Ar list
.Op Fl -pool Ar name
.Op Fl -altroot Ar dir
.Op Fl -swap Ar size
.Op Fl -zone Ar name
.Op Fl -erase
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes
.Ar disk
in the shape every
.Xr softwareupdate 8
update leaves, without asking anything, for UEFI machines:
.Bl -enum
.It
A GPT with a 260 MB FAT32 ESP, optional swap of
.Ar size ,
and one ZFS partition.
There is no BIOS boot partition.
.It
The pool
.Ar name
(default
.Cm rmxroot )
created under the alternate root
.Ar dir
(default
.Pa /mnt )
with
.Cm mountpoint=none ,
.Cm atime=off ,
.Cm compression=lz4
and no cache file.
.It
The catalog's full stream received by softwareupdate's engine onto
.Ar pool Ns /base/ Ns Ar lineage ,
its snapshot cloned to
.Ar pool Ns /ROOT/ Ns Ar snapshot ,
held as
.Cm rmxos-head
and set as the pool's
.Cm bootfs .
.It
Data:
.Ar pool Ns /data
and its
.Cm private ,
.Cm Users
(case-insensitive),
.Cm Library
and
.Cm local ,
with
.Pa /private/etc
populated from the base's template by
.Pa /usr/libexec/rmxos-datasync .
.It
The seeds on Data:
.Pa rc.conf
with the hostname, DHCP on the default interface,
.Cm sshd_enable
and
.Xr mac_do 4 ;
the first user, home
.Pa /Users/ Ns Ar name ,
whose only login is the public key in
.Ar file ,
and who becomes root with
.Xr mdo 1
by a
.Va security.mac.do.rules
line in
.Pa sysctl.conf ;
root's password locked;
.Pa localtime
from
.Ar zone
(default
.Cm UTC ) ;
and the first
.Cm installed
line of the update history.
.It
The environment's
.Pa /boot/loader.efi
at
.Pa EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
and
.Pa efi/freebsd/loader.efi
on the ESP, and
.Pa efi/freebsd/loader.env
holding only the console lines for
.Ar list ,
a comma-separated list of loader consoles
.Pq Cm comconsole , efi , vidconsole , nullconsole , spinconsole .
.El
.Pp
Everything is unmounted and the pool exported at the end; the machine's own
loader imports it.
.Pp
Before any write,
.Nm
refuses a disk that holds the running root, an imported pool, a mount or
swap, a disk that is not empty (it has a partition table, or its first or
last MiB is not zero) unless
.Fl -erase
is given, and a catalog without a full stream.
A failure part-way names what was made, unmounts and exports the pool.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width RMXOS_SU_FIXTURE
.It Ev RMXOS_SU_FIXTURE
A host test directory: only an
.Xr md 4
disk backed by a file below it, an alternate root below it and a pool whose
name starts with
.Cm rmxsu
are accepted.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the disk is written, 1 after a one-line refusal or failure, 2 for a
usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mdo 1 ,
.Xr mac_do 4 ,
.Xr softwareupdate 8 ,
.Xr zpool 8
